<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed stronger at 3.41 pct below parity rate.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed stronger at 3.41 pct below parity rate.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.4800 to the dollar, up from 3.5550 on Tuesday and at 1.9400 to the mark, up from 1.9780, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 3.41 percent below the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, stronger than Tuesday's 5.69 percent fix.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
